# Frontend environment
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the JavaScript bundle at BUILD time.
# That means two things:
#   1. Nothing secret goes in here. Anyone can read these in the shipped bundle.
#   2. Changing a value needs a rebuild, not just a restart.

# Where the API lives. Leave this UNSET in development — Vite proxies /api to
# http://localhost:5000 (see vite.config.js), so a relative path works and there
# is no CORS preflight locally.
#
# In production the API is on a different host, and a relative /api would hit
# the static site and 404. Set the API's absolute origin, including /api:
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://streetpaws-api.onrender.com/api
#
# The backend's CLIENT_ORIGIN must point back at wherever this frontend is
# served from, or the browser will block every request.
# VITE_API_URL=
